{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBU4ZuZBsPkFaJR6upVA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 1 (Pb 0.82 / Sb 0.18)** as the best composition. Its EQE was 0.0074%, the highest of the three I measured.\n\n| Index | Pb / Sb | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 0.82 / 0.18 | 0.0074 |\n| 8 | 0.63 / 0.37 | 0.0067 |\n| 18 | 0.45 / 0.55 | 0.0009 |\n\n- **What XRD showed:** I used 4 of the 5 XRD scans, on indices 1, 8, 14 and 24. A Pb-rich phase (main peak at Q ≈ 2.04 Å⁻¹) dominates at high Pb. A pyrochlore-like Pb₂Sb₂O₇ phase (peaks at Q ≈ 1.88, 2.37, 3.56 Å⁻¹) takes over as Sb increases.\n- **Why the Pb-rich end wins:** the light is 2.1 eV, which is probably below the pyrochlore's band gap, so it absorbs little. The EQE fits this: it falls as Sb rises, sharply once pyrochlore dominates.\n- **What I left out:** I didn't measure the Sb-rich end (indices 20–28). XRD at index 24 is mostly pyrochlore, and EQE was already falling with Sb.\n\nAll three merit measurements are used. Index 0 (Pb 0.83), the most Pb-rich composition, was never measured. The falling trend suggests it could beat index 1, so the true best in the library may be slightly higher than what I found."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":558,"cache_read_input_tokens":9321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":558},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22558a59-822e-4214-a9a3-d1c85216b552","uuid":"4235e30e-8c65-45fa-a194-5f7ca91f7595","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:36:20.537Z","request_id":"req_011CfBU4ZSGyxvZMmccjv8ar"}
